{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.RatioEntireOfSameDivisor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.RatioEntireOfSameDivisor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Meromorphic.NormalForm","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Meromorphic.Order","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RatioEntire.entire_toMeromorphicNFOn_div_of_same_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RatioEntire.entire_toMeromorphicNFOn_div_of_same_order","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RatioEntireOfSameDivisor.lean#L35-L61","doc":"**Same divisor ⇒ entire ratio.** If `Φ, Ψ` are meromorphic on `ℂ`, `Φ` is\nnowhere locally zero (`meromorphicOrderAt Φ ≠ ⊤` everywhere), and they have the\n**same divisor** (`meromorphicOrderAt Ψ = meromorphicOrderAt Φ` at every point),\nthen the normal-form representative `r := toMeromorphicNFOn (Ψ/Φ) univ` is\n**entire** (`Differentiable ℂ r`) and agrees with `Ψ/Φ` on a punctured\nneighbourhood of every point. This is the `hr_entire` divisor-rigidity input of\nthe Faddeev uniqueness leg. ","signatureChunk":0}]}